# Local dev defaults (loaded by `npm start` only — not by builds or tests).
#
# A relative base keeps API calls same-origin, so they hit the dev server's
# /api proxy in vite.config.ts, which forwards to the dev Function App. Going
# direct from the browser would fail CORS: the dev API allows only its paired
# Static Web App origin.
#
# Override for a local func host without editing this file:
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:7071/api npm start
# (shell vars beat .env files in Vite, and an absolute URL bypasses the proxy)
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api

# Entra sign-in (REQ-004) is deliberately NOT configured locally: without the
# VITE_ENTRA_* vars the app runs auth-less — no sign-in screen, no token —
# which keeps quick local dev and the browser-verify tooling working while the
# API's AUTH_ENFORCED stays false. To exercise real sign-in locally, run with
# the dev registration (its redirect allows http://localhost:3000/):
#   VITE_ENTRA_TENANT_ID=d2fa8fd6-d1f2-4ac4-bcf5-e8dd34885bb3 \
#   VITE_ENTRA_SPA_CLIENT_ID=62ab1ce5-45d7-4263-90f5-aa406946e206 \
#   VITE_ENTRA_API_SCOPE=api://5634f56e-8d49-451d-96eb-6d79a6e040b9/access_as_teacher \
#   npm start
# ⚠️ Once AUTH_ENFORCED flips on the dev API (REQ-004 T4), move these out of
# the comment: an auth-less local app will get 401s from the real dev API.
